From 3267234b9fa1657ed7ea13167e7a8d9873e88fcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:15:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 105/105] Font: the menus' packed labels laid out in the font's
 spacing (drawStringPieces)

Rows that a screen copies in pieces cut at the original's offsets were drawn in the original's cells, each glyph centred
in its cell: even but loose with font b ("S t a t u s", the Tech tab's help). drawStringPieces (font.c,
DRAW_STRING_PIECES in dw/mod_font.h) takes the crops' offsets of the row (read from each screen's renderString calls)
and draws each piece with the font's own spacing and kerning, from where its first glyph's original cell started, or
centred in the span its original cells took (PIECE_CENTRE: the tabs, the chart's level names, the centred titles).
Converted: the status, tech, player, medals, card and chart labels, the Tech tab's help lines (only the first is cut),
the stat labels Off/Def, YearDay, the save screens' Yes/No rows, Mojyamon's header, the curling options. The digits row
keeps its cells (renderNumber copies it at 8-pixel steps), and so do the text boxes in cells.
In cells mode a space advances by the glyph before it, as the original did (the calendar's blank grade cells moved the
next grade 4 pixels into the wrong column), and the calendar's first date under 10 no longer adds a space after the
figure space that pads it (the dates of days 1-9 shifted 8 pixels).
